.SH NAME
messq-completion - emit the shell completion script (bash, zsh or fish)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq completion  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Emit the completion script for the named shell. Source it in your
shell's startup file, e.g.:

.PP
source <(messq completion bash)

.PP
Completion never blocks a shell: live stream and consumer names are
fetched on a 200ms budget, and a dead or unauthorised daemon simply
completes nothing, silently.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for completion


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


